{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"107414","commit":"496a2448383e0316baf22f3f3605daee2061682f","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The logic for handling foldable expressions in `surrogate()` methods seems correct but could be simplified and made more consistent. For example, the `Count` class checks if the field is a `Literal` and not a list before returning `null`, while `CountDistinct` directly returns a new expression without such checks. Consider standardizing this behavior across similar methods.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java-2365:2469-2523:2540,2549:2569,2586:2775","promptId":"#73AKB","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":2365,"endPos":2469,"startLine":66,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":66,"endLineOffset":119,"length":105}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2523,"endPos":2540,"startLine":68,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":68,"endLineOffset":25,"length":18},{"pos":2549,"endPos":2569,"startLine":69,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":69,"endLineOffset":28,"length":21},{"pos":2586,"endPos":2775,"startLine":71,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":73,"endLineOffset":118,"length":190}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java--3407:4400","promptId":"#0VTRR","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","srcChanges":[],"ds